The '''physics of respiration''' encompasses the physical principles and laws that govern gas exchange and breathing mechanics in living organisms. Respiration is fundamentally a [[biophysical]] process governed by classical [[gas laws]], [[fluid dynamics]], [[thermodynamics]], and [[mechanics]].<ref name="West2021">{{cite book |last1=West |first1=John B. |last2=Luks |first2=Andrew M. |title=West's Respiratory Physiology: The Essentials |date=2021 |publisher=Wolters Kluwer |edition=11th |isbn=978-1975139186}}</ref><ref name="Levitzky2022">{{cite book |last=Levitzky |first=Michael G. |title=Pulmonary Physiology |date=2022 |publisher=McGraw Hill |edition=10th |isbn=1264270046}}</ref>

