'''Jim Carrey's artwork''' includes [[paintings]], [[sculptures]], [[mixed-media]] pieces and [[satirical]] drawings. [[Jim Carrey|Carrey]] developed an interest in [[visual art]] during his childhood, but mostly set his artistic pursuits aside during the height of his acting career before resuming them more seriously around 2010–2011. In 2011, he held his first solo exhibition, featuring approximately forty paintings, sculptures and mixed-media pieces.

Following the [[2016 United States presidential election]], Carrey began posting satirical drawings that criticised [[Donald Trump]] and [[First presidency of Donald Trump#Administration|his first administration]]. He also directed his satire towards [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] politicians, the [[National Rifle Association]] and authoritarian leaders abroad. His political cartoons were shown in the exhibitions ''IndigNATION'' in 2018 and ''This Light Never Goes Out'' in 2019.

