'''Charles Ray Tolbert''' (November 14, 1936 – December 4, 2025) was an American [[astronomer]] and [[Professor Emeritus]] at the [[University of Virginia]], known for his contributions to [[optical astronomy]] and [[radio astronomy]], his dedication to undergraduate astronomy education, and his leadership in professional scientific organizations.<ref name="obituary">{{cite web |url=https://www.dignitymemorial.com/obituaries/charlottesville-va/charles-tolbert-12657035 |title=Charles Ray Tolbert Obituary |publisher=Teague Funeral Service |location=Charlottesville, Virginia |date=December 2025 |access-date=2026-04-02}}</ref><ref name="uvatoday">{{cite web |url=https://news.virginia.edu/content/astronomer-tolbert-wins-emmons-award-excellence-teaching |title=Astronomer Tolbert Wins Emmons Award for Excellence in Teaching |publisher=UVA Today |date=July 3, 2013 |access-date=2026-04-02 |archive-date=2024-08-18 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240818122757/https://news.virginia.edu/content/astronomer-tolbert-wins-emmons-award-excellence-teaching |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite book |url=https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/1635/chapter/14 |title=Working Papers: Astronomy and Astrophysics Panel Reports (1991) |language=en}}</ref>

